摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Session settings, MCP servers, and Skill management plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Web GUI.","id":"gh:1336634168","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-session-settings","slug":"u9521/dsh-session-settings","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Session settings, MCP servers, and Skill management plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Web GUI."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-session-settings"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Session Settings, MCP Server, and Skill Management plugin for DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Web GUI.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Configure per-session or global settings directly from the Web GUI with immediate effect:\n1. **Subag"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ent Model & Reasoning Effort**: Independently configure provider, model, and reasoning effort for su"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"bagents (`subagent`, `subagent_fork`, `workflow`).\n2. **Centralized MCP Server Management**: First-c"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"lass sidebar navigation item for Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers with 2-stage compatibility pro"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"bing, automatic protocol downgrade, tool schema inspection, and read-only browsing of resources and "},{"id":"p5s6","text":"prompts.\n3. **Session-Level MCP Tool Control**: Granularly enable/disable MCP servers and specific t"},{"id":"p5s7","text":"ools per session or follow global defaults.\n4. **Session-Level Skill Management & Control**: Indepen"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"dently enable/disable bundled, user, and project skills per session, with automatic dynamic prompt c"},{"id":"p5s9","text":"atalog filtering and execution enforcement."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Settings Sidebar Navigation Entry**: Top-level section in Settings navigation sidebar (dedicated"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" icon) for direct MCP server management.\n- **Session-Specific Tab**: Dedicated tab in the conversati"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"on view for configuring the active session's subagent models, MCP tools, and skills.\n- **Switch-Base"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"d Subagent Control**: Three explicit switches — allow agents to choose a subagent model, replace the"},{"id":"p7s5","text":" model of forked subagents, and specify a subagent model with its reasoning effort.\n- **Instant Effe"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"ct**: Each agent's scope layers are re-declared on save and on tool-registry changes, so an updated "},{"id":"p7s7","text":"policy applies on the very next request without restarting DSH.\n- **Three Explicit Scopes**: Session"},{"id":"p7s8","text":", Workspace, and Global are distinct write targets chosen on the page, never inferred from which fie"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"lds a request happens to carry.\n- **New-Session Page Targets a Live Session**: Choosing a workspace "},{"id":"p7s10","text":"on the New-Session page connects that workspace's blank session, and the modal writes session-scope "},{"id":"p7s11","text":"edits straight to it — effective on the next request. A page with no session has no session scope to"},{"id":"p7s12","text":" write to, so that tab disables itself and explains why.\n- **Single Interface Contract**: Paths, HTT"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"P methods, and request bodies are each declared once in `src/types.ts`; the client sends and the ser"},{"id":"p7s14","text":"ver validates against the same definitions, with no server-side compatibility branches.\n- **One Reso"},{"id":"p7s15","text":"lution Ladder**: The session → workspace → global rules and their defaults live in `src/shared/`, sh"},{"id":"p7s16","text":"ared by the panel that displays them and the server that enforces them, so a panel cannot show one v"},{"id":"p7s17","text":"alue while enforcement uses another.\n- **Authenticated Routes**: All routes are registered on the of"},{"id":"p7s18","text":"ficial connection carrier, so a request passes the Host/Origin fence and browser authentication befo"},{"id":"p7s19","text":"re any handler runs.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Sharing sandbox directory lists"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**Export to clipboard** in the sandbox panel writes the current draft as plain text:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"One `path | description` row per line; the first `#` line is an optional title; blank lines and furt"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"her `#` lines are ignored. Everything after the first `|` belongs to the description, so a descripti"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"on may contain one. A row without `|` is a bare path."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Paste that text into **Manage presets → Import from clipboard** to store it as a preset, or hand it "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"to someone else. Readers accept the format by hand, so the shape above is what any tool producing it"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"else. Readers accept the format by hand, so the shape above is what any tool producing it must emit."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Mainline Compatibility"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Plugin Branch | Compatible DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Mainline | Architecture & Features |\n| :--- | :-"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"-- | :--- |\n| **`main` branch** | **`>= 0.2.2-rc.1`** | Native support for **Session Format V4**, **"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"Cordis 4.1**, `@modelcontextprotocol/client` 2.2.0, the `agent.model.select()` routing API, the `San"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"dboxPolicy.additionalWritableRoots` channel, the `settings.section.icon` slot, and the `ui-primitive"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"itionalWritableRoots` channel, the `settings.section.icon` slot, and the `ui-primitives` icon set. |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"> **⚠️ Note**: The `main` branch targets DSH 0.2.2-rc.1 and above natively. It keeps **no backward-c"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ompatibility shims** and does not support earlier DSH lines. The host does not read `engines.dsh`; c"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ompatibility is enforced through the `peerDependencies` range on `@deepseek-ai/dsh`, so an incompati"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"ble host refuses the plugin instead of loading it half-broken."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### 🚀 One-Line Quick Install (Recommended)"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"This repository includes a GitHub Actions workflow that automatically builds and deploys a minimal r"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"elease to the `dist` branch (containing built artifacts and manifests without raw source bloat)."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"You can install this plugin with a single command without any local build step:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"> **Note**: After installation, start or restart the Web service:\n>\n[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Installation from Source (For Developers)"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"#### Step 1: Obtain the Source Code"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Clone the repository to your local machine:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"#### Step 2: Install Dependencies & Build"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"#### Step 3: Register to DSH Web Profile"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"##### Verify Installation\nList the plugins in the `web` profile to verify that `@local/dsh-session-s"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ettings` is registered:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"#### Step 4: Start and Verify"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Plugin Updates & Upgrades"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"### Option 1: Online Update (Recommended)"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"If you installed via the one-line command from the GitHub dist branch, update directly using `dsh pl"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"ugin --profile web update`:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"> **Note**: After updating, start or restart the Web service:\n>\n[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### Q2: What happens if I save session settings before the session exists?\n**A**: On the New-Session"},{"id":"p39s2","text":" page a blank session already exists as soon as a workspace is connected, so session-scope edits are"},{"id":"p39s3","text":" written to that session and take effect on the next request. On a page with no session at all there"},{"id":"p39s4","text":" is nothing to write to: the Session tab is disabled and a note beside the tabs says so. Workspace a"},{"id":"p39s5","text":"nd Global defaults remain editable there. Nothing is ever staged or retargeted — a save lands only o"},{"id":"p39s6","text":"n the scope you selected."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
